Note, a login flow with a form, a session and a cookie.
Note, start it, then open localhost 8090 in your browser.
Note, run this from the project folder so that the pages are found.

Let visits be 0.

Before every request, do the following.
Add 1 to visits.
End before.

Define show form that takes request, do the following.
Read the file examples slash login.html and store it in page.
Set content type to html.
Respond with the value of page.
End define.

Define handle login that takes request, do the following.
Let user be the form value username of request.
Start a session for request.
Set the session value name in request to the value of user.
Set the cookie username of request to the value of user.
Respond with Welcome to your account.
End define.

Define show profile that takes request, do the following.
Let who be the session value name of request.
Let remembered be the cookie username of request.
Create a dictionary called profile.
Set the entry session name in profile to the value of who.
Set the entry cookie name in profile to the value of remembered.
Set the entry requests so far in profile to the value of visits.
Respond with the value of profile.
End define.

Add route GET slash to show form.
Add route POST slash login to handle login.
Add route GET slash profile to show profile.

Start a webserver on port 8090.
Say Open localhost 8090 in your browser.
Wait for connections.
